us on the bottom micro  fundamentals but i think i suspect the  problem with a lot of investors watching  the problem with a lot of investors who  came into this week and are having a bad  week is that they spent entirely too  much time focusing on the the bottom-up  fundamentals and not nearly enough time  either focusing on or allocating um to  resources like myself  and so when you look at something like  uh bitcoin let's go to the micro factors  uh obviously there's been a ton of talk  about uh realized price for kind of the  on-chain cost basis i think last week  you had told us that anywhere around  that like 28 000 range you'd get start  getting excited uh we obviously breached  28 000 got down to you know somewhere in  that 25 000 range realize price seems to  be around 24 000 how are you thinking  about these and full well understanding  like now we're talking about micro  improvements of uh you know various  prices of a couple thousand dollars but  but how do you think about where we are  and some of the price action that's  occurred uh given the models you guys  have  yeah so i would actually say it's quite  encouraging that we held so um if you  look at the uh fibonacci retracement  analysis that i put out on twitter  yesterday um relative to uh the to the  entire bull run from the lows that you  and palina were talking about just prior  to my coming on to the highs that we uh  observed uh last fall you know the 61.8  retracement level which has been a you  know a very sort of um sound level to  kind of invest in speculating bitcoin in  throughout the throughout its life cycle  you know that level's at 28 774 and so  we kind of breached below that and now  we're trading right back above it so  it's clear that other investors are  keying off that level and saying hey  this is a good price to buy now the re  and so i do believe that is still a  reasonable price to buy the problem with  we're buying it today is that we're not  yet near that sort of inflecti